# Section background rhythm

On service, обръщане, and similar long content pages, **no section may use the same background as the section directly above or below it**.

## Allowed bands

Use the existing classes only:

- `trim-band--mist` — soft gray
- `trim-band--white` — plain white
- `trim-band--lined` — white with subtle diagonal lines
- `trim-band--charcoal` — dark accent band (banners)

## Cycle

Prefer: **mist → white → mist → lined → (repeat)**.

Charcoal / contact dark bands break the cycle intentionally; resume with a band that differs from both neighbors.

## Do / Don't

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: transparent overrides the band; neighbors look the same -->
<section class="trim-section trim-price-section trim-band--white">
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.trim-price-section { background: transparent; }
```

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: two whites in a row -->
<section class="trim-section trim-band--white">...</section>
<section class="trim-offer-banner trim-band--white">...</section>
```

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<section class="trim-section trim-band--white">...</section>
<section class="trim-offer-banner trim-band--mist">...</section>
<section class="trim-section trim-band--lined">...</section>
```

When sections are optional, assign the next band from the cycle only for sections that actually render so the visible stack still alternates.
